data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":3127,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0a50c8dc540dd4c8016adf720b73008191a18dc0b1144872b3","object":"response","created_at":1793028620,"completed_at":1793028657,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You translate the supplied natural-language proof faithfully into Lean 4. Use the explicit project premises and any proved result in the pinned Mathlib environment. Preserve all assumptions, conclusions, equality modes and the supplied proof route. No reference answers, personal context, other tasks, shell or external services are available. Use the submit tool when the requested artifact is complete; if rejected, repair it. A strategy is advice, never an additional theorem or assumption.\n\n# Lean implementation safeguards\n\nApply these requirements within the accepted NL0 and the fixed Lean interface.\nThey govern implementation, not additional NL0 detail or a weaker Audit B.\nUse existing library readers and local checking tools; no separate review\nmodel, new premise or mandatory lookup of every familiar declaration is needed.\n\n1. **Check critical library signatures.** Before relying on a critical or\n   unfamiliar library application, establish its complete type in the pinned\n   environment, including explicit, implicit and instance binders and all\n   side conditions. Read the declaration or check a small typed application\n   when its signature is uncertain. Do not infer the calling convention from\n   its name or pass an implicit argument as though it were an explicit one.\n   A previously checked signature in this context need not be looked up again.\n2. **Constrain difficult inference.** When coercions or implicit inference\n   obscure the intended application, give the intermediate fact an explicit\n   type and supply the relevant named parameters, such as the set, exponent\n   or ambient space. Prefer this to leaving Lean to discover those choices by\n   unfolding large definitions. Routine unambiguous arguments can stay\n   implicit; explicit parameters must preserve the existing target and inputs.\n3. **Check conversions before combining them.** When an argument crosses Lean\n   representations, first establish a small typed conversion fact, then use\n   it in the main proof. In particular, distinguish `ℝ`, `ℝ≥0` and `ℝ≥0∞`;\n   check the conversion direction, nonnegativity and any finiteness conditions.\n   A conversion is not automatically invertible, and matching notation does\n   not establish equality of differently typed expressions. Reuse a checked\n   fact when available. Do not invent another representation, a global helper\n   requirement or an extra hypothesis just to satisfy this instruction.\n4. **Isolate an inference failure.** If compiler feedback identifies a library\n   application, coercion or expensive inference problem, reduce the next check\n   to that application or conversion with explicit local types before adding\n   more proof code. Use `check_auxiliary` in a proof worker, or\n   `check_lean_types` during preparation when that tool is supplied. Helpers\n   use only the current allowed inputs and never become new premises. Once\n   the small check succeeds, integrate the result and recheck the complete\n   obligation; success of a helper alone does not accept the target.\n\nThese rules do not interrupt an active compiler call or impose a time limit.\nThey guide the next implementation/checking action when feedback is available.\nRetain failed attempts and actual diagnostics. Standalone assembly, native\ntrust/signature checks and independent endpoint-fidelity Audit B remain required.\n End this stage immediately when a submit tool reports stage_complete:true; the controller handles later stages. Within a proof stage, checked helper attempts are available through read_lean_draft. After a context reset, query its index before claiming no draft or helper exists. Helpers never become new premises. Use familiar interfaces directly; no background-note scan is required. For a relevant obstacle, select a matching local background_note_index entry and read_background_note if its details may help. Relate the actual Lean goal/context to its NL step: use the note grounds to identify a small missing application premise or transport, prove it from permitted inputs, then check the intended application. Verify actual types and conditions; a note is not a Lean proof or extra assumption. If it does not fit, continue ordinary allowed search or repair without insisting on that note or rebuilding a larger argument by default.","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0a50c8dc540dd4c8016adf72102028819193f5f5b3ecf9accf","summary":[],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq33IQvOP1P1TMhANtRZRqlYRuFKihi5J-Wkxn95c5EwiVta8uMfwsBivs2XtBVc8i28fAiL6pP1UBbj-XVTlEfqi8B06vGbeg6AM-PUxz-j5hqb1HiIYEJUom--oXTd5bZVMnK7q1-sr2R3BDkE92H9ECw6V1FY8yE5Pa4jnBRAI-favxMl6kKD1I_pyhmi4rhnGb94a902HXdwEX4g_3suMLBtrYRBnRvDS6BOYZEYwhod7iz1VxwD4g2_Kh0_GRCC1bS2-7LwBrej8pDtwxgw-z3vnvjFc6v5Kel1-8oGvfgPI6rlCLrYm4CHoqeVxIE_0iP0Gr-SkGt_SUSOTnHGXaUwrDjejPPXjNVukz9G37X9AvR7gdHezMtdQcjvSXD9JN9hGDh6ZevdanTbEfLWtG6RRy94oxSAsLJdgCB1Bo3P3DMr3b_HHWB8pcYFNS7qaal0IOoSVpMQqiMsjvL4mDXwJIuKCsRiWE9nOoMEONwysEI1-JzoWPVA0aDlB_ilp_SPFoUO5sKXfqh8NiiU2z5YGuwgs8jx8hY0J3tO_EjvX20JOz29329kV_ION7Ejd4hGn1aMUAFhwF41U9rSGMvbMm3Wyr3tkU-b5iENy2zY21qDCvWSlivfl5XYjqMik9ivnZfuQC8rV1tAaI6KANfz9A0FzNc-xTg_ETHQz33IOjX04E_uJiW-9e3ytcICS1-etd3VmqflDhLKsXnWpdEk149UYggyn730Y54CYtCeizjgAyyDorq9NknFsbNwv0mkSQSbEYwwvslcCKjVUvgwPoh7j95xWLHQrNySwHPVlk0ojVZ7qWV1xIGW9c1EakmzXg3iwDGErVXXj1mjliUhU_RMQ5f8oBNz5TVcCQyoN3jr6hONnFYuCtIgCtuMlcxP9U3Dkl6M6r39adLBNJhJl9fh3W32HKIJvOJLoT9gNtdVurbHIIqcyjPFzukcnYkH6FJyl8lEuE7HHftA6z43oWV6dp2IcX5jOPvXNyp6TD0U5PsjkzY7H929S4C9hYf7iURwcH4WMhuxbncsHzVyaT0bql9Yk9BIceBTtONneKY2y8JMSm51eD9fF55oXJ5sLv_qPkOte1q3rmvsMHII65QnQ_h_fvCWMwUE7d3rPRGbIcsECi36bbLAGF3n3gMweEid8X_T_t-WZfRDeMfXK90oDK5AxvqzCuEDENknOW22rcIysMp13cE9Gz5EEaihwBkuviNG_7axDcxiSl_CclfDJMwZzcD29QzGst7XyqOuRKdPVu47GBI5z5MaanJG02SLStsuZWvUmpvNrGT5C5bYH6DLrxWXIxxSqL32WUCNEtxlK1zT_F1Zy0B093YqV6VkJFAQoxrF-vfT6zdzsHirC24ujOok_nkxgkywxln64zkcMwXmyTfXmGz0UcuBh1winNJEX0P7QRm1oql6kKMXZnm2hzIUhswE8UgscQzT8bSPibOFNNtsjWImjf8PiqZ6wI_m1SFNu8rKyhNtq891BAA-OiLLQG70xqetiycMJ-YOZoNM_OQJrarnEeaUutKKBvfRjtwiWJLEB6-P36QSsgJbTYalwUIsZPQR-8Tb_7umQC9mLH4Qd2-BJ9MY523HwD3A6CtSZ6lyPgu7nx_s-SE0a4PmxxzjWS3wmLL3oopJ-qcz55hntRBFtdmoi_9Ivlo6n6EcOjh9rLX6ARUBT5SLcgK8MH_ST0jijLZkG6gKQBgTxGdNvMV_amlIKxzBw-1CWFnpLxD0E0fZzWnftqYOOctAPAj1RDPnTM4kKGfRt3ITHpvWWETLlUGv9CgDQnrVCu9ymoPvX9TDk42gSf30-9PD-CBzwI9qnZkYbOUfKRYywL66pHxrw6gKhTZoM09Yau3FvRXAHWPftlOIR_COIGa_FnZcvlQ_2ikI8TLJPbQ9osjwb2IKXHDQipa1W1joSeVx-d8fs7oIC1ojygL_iK6Oo_CotEk0IU1aiF9NMivfX6-QiFO3JqA5i6iYROW4HwICNh8ogsfZaUnQUDQLePFH0k2oJRIgADew5uHbX2cdGGvoNfFgVQh6QKfPtNknS2-jqxMo6GneRHu4Dk_lMGV9Ct-9G472k="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0a50c8dc540dd4c8016adf72104318819182a3b371d5923869","call_id":"call_128280f3088c426f87e670ef57c7302b","name":"check_transition","arguments":"{\"proof\":\"classical\\nintro hn q δ ε hq hδ hε\\nhave hqpos : 0 < q := ENNReal.ofReal_pos.mp (lt_of_le_of_lt bot_le hq)\\nhave hp : 0 ≤ q + 1 := by linarith\\nhave hs : 0 < Real.sqrt 2 := Real.sqrt_pos.2 (by norm_num)\\nlet r := min 1 (δ / Real.sqrt 2)\\nhave hr : 0 < r := lt_min (by norm_num) (div_pos hδ hs)\\nhave hr1 : r ≤ 1 := min_le_left _ _\\nhave hrδ : Real.sqrt 2 * r ≤ δ := by\\n  have h := min_le_right (1 : ℝ) (δ / Real.sqrt 2)\\n  simpa only [mul_comm] using (le_div_iff₀ hs).1 h\\nobtain ⟨U, hU, hUpos, hcost⟩ := h_T007 hn q r ε hq hr hr1 hε\\nlet d : ℕ → ℝ := fun i => (Metric.ediam (U i)).toReal\\nhave hfin (i : ℕ) : Metric.ediam (U i) ≠ ∞ := ne_top_of_le_ne_top ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top (hU.2 i)\\nhave hd0 (i : ℕ) : 0 ≤ d i := ENNReal.toReal_nonneg\\nhave hdle (i : ℕ) : d i ≤ r := ENNReal.toReal_le_of_le_ofReal hr.le (hU.2 i)\\nhave hdeq (i : ℕ) : ENNReal.ofReal (d i) = Metric.ediam (U i) := ENNReal.ofReal_toReal (hfin i)\\nhave hdpos (i : ℕ) (hi : (U i).Nonempty) : 0 < d i := ENNReal.toReal_pos (ne_of_gt (hUpos i hi)) (hfin i)\\nlet N : ℕ → ℕ := fun i => ⌈1 / d i⌉₊\\nhave hN (i : ℕ) (hi : (U i).Nonempty) : 0 < N i ∧ 1 / (N i : ℝ) ≤ d i ∧ (N i : ℝ) ≤ 2 / d i := by\\n  have hd := hdpos i hi\\n  have hNr : (0 : ℝ) < N i := lt_of_lt_of_le (one_div_pos.mpr hd) (Nat.le_ceil (1 / d i))\\n  refine ⟨by exact_mod_cast hNr, ?_, ?_⟩\\n  · apply (div_le_iff₀ hNr).2\\n    have h := (div_le_iff₀ hd).1 (Nat.le_ceil (1 / d i))\\n    nlinarith\\n  · have h := (Nat.ceil_lt_add_one (le_of_lt (one_div_pos.mpr hd))).le\\n    calc\\n      (N i : ℝ) ≤ 1 / d i + 1 := h\\n      _ ≤ 2 / d i := by\\n        apply (le_div_iff₀ hd).2\\n        have hdi : d i ≤ 1 := (hdle i).trans hr1\\n        field_simp\\n        nlinarith\\nhave partition : ∀ (M : ℕ), 0 < M → ∀ t ∈ unitI, ∃ j : ℕ, j < M ∧ t ∈ Set.Icc ((j : ℝ) / M) (((j : ℝ) + 1) / M) := by\\n  intro M hM t ht\\n  have hMr : (0 : ℝ) < M := by exact_mod_cast hM\\n  change 0 ≤ t ∧ t ≤ 1 at ht\\n  by_cases ht1 : t = 1\\n  · refine ⟨M - 1, by omega, ?_⟩\\n    have hcast : ((M - 1 : ℕ) : ℝ) + 1 = M := by exact_mod_cast Nat.sub_add_cancel hM\\n    rw [ht1]\\n    constructor\\n    · apply (div_le_iff₀ hMr).2\\n      linarith\\n    · rw [hcast, div_self (ne_of_gt hMr)]\\n  · have htlt : t < 1 := lt_of_le_of_ne ht.2 ht1\\n    refine ⟨⌊t * M⌋₊, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩\\n    · apply (Nat.floor_lt (mul_nonneg ht.1 hMr.le)).2\\n      nlinarith\\n    · exact (div_le_iff₀ hMr).2 (Nat.floor_le (mul_nonneg ht.1 hMr.le))\\n    · exact (le_div_iff₀ hMr).2 (Nat.lt_floor_add_one (t * M)).le\\nhave geom : ∀ (a b : W n) (c : ℝ), 0 ≤ c → dist (projX n a) (projX n b) ≤ c → dist (projT n a) (projT n b) ≤ c → dist a b ≤ Real.sqrt 2 * c := by\\n  intro a b c hc hx ht\\n  have hid : dist a b ^ 2 = dist (projX n a) (projX n b) ^ 2 + dist (projT n a) (projT n b) ^ 2 := by\\n    rw [EuclideanSpace.dist_sq_eq a b, EuclideanSpace.dist_sq_eq (projX n a) (projX n b)]\\n    simp [projX, projT, Fintype.sum_sum_type]\\n  have hs2 : (Real.sqrt 2) ^ 2 = (2 : ℝ) := Real.sq_sqrt (by norm_num)\\n  have hx2 : dist (projX n a) (projX n b) ^ 2 ≤ c ^ 2 := (sq_le_sq₀ dist_nonneg hc).2 hx\\n  have ht2 : dist (projT n a) (projT n b) ^ 2 ≤ c ^ 2 := (sq_le_sq₀ dist_nonneg hc).2 ht\\n  have hnon : 0 ≤ Real.sqrt 2 * c := mul_nonneg hs.le hc\\n  nlinarith [dist_nonneg (x := a) (y := b), sq_nonneg (Real.sqrt 2 * c - dist a b)]\\nlet T : ℕ → ℕ → Set (W n) := fun i j => if j < N i then {z | projX n z ∈ U i ∧ projT n z ∈ Set.Icc ((j : ℝ) / N i) (((j : ℝ) + 1) / N i)} else ∅\\nhave hTdiam (i j : ℕ) : Metric.ediam (T i j) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (Real.sqrt 2 * d i) := by\\n  apply Metric.ediam_le_of_forall_dist_le\\n  intro a ha b hb\\n  by_cases hj : j < N i\\n  · simp only [T, if_pos hj, Set.mem_setOf_eq] at ha hb\\n    apply geom a b (d i) (hd0 i)\\n    · exact Metric.dist_le_diam_of_mem' (hfin i) ha.1 hb.1\\n    · have hinv := (hN i ⟨projX n a, ha.1⟩).2.1\\n      have hlen : ((j : ℝ) + 1) / (N i : ℝ) - (j : ℝ) / N i = 1 / (N i : ℝ) := by ring\\n      rw [Real.dist_eq, abs_le]\\n      constructor <;> linarith [ha.2.1, ha.2.2, hb.2.1, hb.2.2]\\n  · simp [T, hj] at ha\\nlet e : ℕ ≃ ℕ × ℕ := Nat.pairEquiv.symm\\nlet B : ℕ → Set (W n) := fun k => T (e k).1 (e k).2\\nhave hB : IsCover δ (cyl n E) B := by\\n  constructor\\n  · intro z hz\\n    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp (hU.1 hz.1)\\n    obtain ⟨j, hj, ht⟩ := partition (N i) (hN i ⟨projX n z, hi⟩).1 (projT n z) hz.2\\n    apply Set.mem_iUnion.mpr\\n    refine ⟨e.symm (i,j), ?_⟩\\n    simpa [B, T, hj] using And.intro hi ht\\n  · intro k\\n    exact (hTdiam _ _).trans (ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal ((mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hdle _) hs.le).trans hrδ))\\nlet C : ℝ := 2 * (Real.sqrt 2) ^ (q + 1)\\nhave hC : 0 ≤ C := by dsimp [C]; positivity\\nhave powbound (i : ℕ) (hi : (U i).Nonempty) : (N i : ℝ≥0∞) * (ENNReal.ofReal (Real.sqrt 2 * d i)) ^ (q + 1) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal C * (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ q := by\\n  have hd := hdpos i hi\\n  have hpow : (N i : ℝ) * (Real.sqrt 2 * d i) ^ (q + 1) ≤ C * (d i) ^ q := by\\n    calc\\n      (N i : ℝ) * (Real.sqrt 2 * d i) ^ (q + 1) ≤ (2 / d i) * (Real.sqrt 2 * d i) ^ (q + 1) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hN i hi).2.2 (Real.rpow_nonneg (by positivity) _)\\n      _ = _ := by dsimp [C]; rw [Real.mul_rpow hs.le hd.le, Real.rpow_add_one hd.ne']; field_simp\\n  have hconv1 : ENNReal.ofReal ((N i : ℝ) * (Real.sqrt 2 * d i) ^ (q + 1)) = (N i : ℝ≥0∞) * (ENNReal.ofReal (Real.sqrt 2 * d i)) ^ (q + 1) := by\\n    rw [ENNReal.ofReal_mul (by positivity), ENNReal.ofReal_rpow_of_pos (mul_pos hs hd)]\\n    simp\\n  have hconv2 : ENNReal.ofReal (C * (d i) ^ q) = ENNReal.ofReal C * (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ q := by\\n    rw [ENNReal.ofReal_mul hC, ← ENNReal.ofReal_rpow_of_pos hd, hdeq i]\\n  rw [← hconv1, ← hconv2]\\n  exact ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal hpow\\nhave inner (i : ℕ) : (∑' j, ⨆ (_ : (T i j).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (T i j)) ^ (q + 1)) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal C * (⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ q) := by\\n  by_cases hi : (U i).Nonempty\\n  · simp only [ciSup_pos hi]\\n    apply le_trans (b := (N i : ℝ≥0∞) * (ENNReal.ofReal (Real.sqrt 2 * d i)) ^ (q + 1)) ?_ (powbound i hi)\\n    calc\\n      (∑' j, ⨆ (_ : (T i j).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (T i j)) ^ (q + 1)) ≤ ∑' j, if j < N i then (ENNReal.ofReal (Real.sqrt 2 * d i)) ^ (q + 1) else 0 := by\\n        apply ENNReal.tsum_le_tsum\\n        intro j\\n        by_cases hj : j < N i\\n        · rw [if_pos hj]\\n          exact iSup_le fun _ => ENNReal.rpow_le_rpow (hTdiam i j) hp\\n        · simp [T, hj]\\n      _ = _ := by\\n        rw [tsum_eq_sum (s := Finset.range (N i)) (fun j hj => by simp only [Finset.mem_range] at hj; simp [hj])]\\n        simp [Finset.sum_ite, Finset.filter_true_of_mem, Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]\\n  · have hempty : U i = ∅ := Set.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.mp hi\\n    have hTempty (j : ℕ) : T i j = ∅ := by ext z; simp [T, hempty]\\n    simp [hTempty, hi]\\nhave hBcost : coverCost (q + 1) B ≤ ENNReal.ofReal C * coverCost q U := by\\n  unfold coverCost\\n  change (∑' k, (fun p : ℕ × ℕ => ⨆ (_ : (T p.1 p.2).Nonempty), Metric.ediam (T p.1 p.2) ^ (q + 1)) (e k)) ≤ _\\n  rw [e.tsum_eq (fun p : ℕ × ℕ => ⨆ (_ : (T p.1 p.2).Nonempty), Metric.ediam (T p.1 p.2) ^ (q + 1)), ENNReal.tsum_prod']\\n  exact (ENNReal.tsum_le_tsum inner).trans_eq ENNReal.tsum_mul_left\\ncalc\\n  Hscale (q + 1) δ (cyl n E) ≤ coverCost (q + 1) B := iInf_le_of_le B (iInf_le_of_le hB le_rfl)\\n  _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal C * coverCost q U := hBcost\\n  _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal C * ENNReal.ofReal ε := mul_le_mul_left' hcost.le _\\n  _ = ENNReal.ofReal (2 * (Real.sqrt 2) ^ (q + 1) * ε) := (ENNReal.ofReal_mul hC).symm\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"Search the pinned mathlib Lean source using a regular expression; at most 100 lines.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"Read specified lines of a Mathlib/*.lean source file from the pinned checkout.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_transition","description":"Compile a tactic body for the fixed target; no leading by, declarations, or placeholders.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"proof":{"type":"string"}},"required":["proof"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_transition","description":"Submit and check the final tactic body for the same target.","parameters"